>When I tried to sh the umoria archives #6 & #9, one
>file was uncompressed, then an "unexpected end-of-file"
>message appeared.
There was a problem with some of the files not having a linefeed
at the end.  This caused the END_OF_FILE marker to be appended to
the last line instead of being on a line by itself.  The solution
seems to be:  find all occurences of END_OF_FILE and insert a LF
where required.  After unsharing delete the LF from the end of the
relevant files.  Vi doesn't allow that, but Emacs does.

In summary, this seems to be a bug in shar.
